  "query_preview": "below for more details.\n\nShould finally see some clearing skies sweep W to E across the \narea this morning and allow for much more sunshine later today \ncompared to the past few days. Temperatures remain very mild \nthis morning for mid November (mostly lower 50s!), and with the\nadded sunshine, expect high temperatures to top out well into \nthe 60s for the entire area this afternoon. Wouldn't rule out \nsome lower 70s in our typically-warmest far SW counties as \nwinds veer along and behind a surface trough. The middle third \nof the area from roughly Phillipsburg to the Tri-Cities up \ntoward Fullerton will have the \"nicest\" combination of warm \ntemperatures and lower winds during the afternoon hours.\n\nHave ramped up the mention of fog in the forecast for roughly\nthe southern half of the forecast area late tonight and into\nThursday morning. The surface front/trough that moves into the\narea today will likely stall out and gradually return northward\nduring the day Thursday. Modest moisture pooling along the\nfront/trough axis, in conjunction with mostly clear skies and\nlight winds, could promote a band of fog between roughly I-80 on\nthe north side and I-70 on the south side. Latest REFS shows a\n50-70% chance this fog could be dense with visibilities of ~1/2\nmi, or less.",
